"[2512.15384v1] MedNuggetizer: Confidence-Based Information Nugget Extraction from Medical Documents (https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15384v1)\nciteturn6520view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 8 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15384v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 199\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:  cite63†Image: Cornell University L3: \nL4:  We gratefully acknowledge support from the Simons Foundation, cite1†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , and all contributors. cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org L5: \nL6: cite64†Image: arxiv logo > cite3†cs > arXiv:2512.15384v1\nL7: \nL8: cite4†Help†info.arxiv.org | cite5†Advanced Search L9: \nL10:  All fields Title Author Abstract Comments Journal reference ACM classification MSC classification Report number arXiv identifier DOI ORCID arXiv author ID Help pages Full text\nL11: \nL12: Search\nL13: cite65†Image: arXiv logo L14: \nL15: cite6† †www.cornell.edu L16: \nL17:  open search\nL18: \nL19: GO\nL20: \nL21: open navigation menu\nL22: ## quick links\nL23: \nL24:   * cite7†Login L25:   * cite4†Help Pages†info.arxiv.org L26:   * cite8†About†info.arxiv.org L27: \nL28: # Computer Science > Information Retrieval\nL29: \nL30: arXiv:2512.15384v1 (cs)\nL31: \nL32: [Submitted on 17 Dec 2025]\nL33: # Title:MedNuggetizer: Confidence-Based Information Nugget Extraction from Medical Documents\nL34: \nL35: Authors:cite9†Gregor Donabauer , cite10†Samy Ateia , cite11†Udo Kruschwitz , cite12†Maximilian Burger , cite13†Matthias May , cite14†Christian Gilfrich , cite15†Maximilian Haas , cite16†Julio Ruben Rodas Garzaro , cite17†Christoph Eckl L36: \nL37: View a PDF of the paper titled MedNuggetizer: Confidence-Based Information Nugget Extraction from Medical Documents, by Gregor Donabauer and 8 other authors\nL38: \nL39: cite18†View PDF cite19†HTML (experimental) L40: > Abstract:We present MedNuggetizer, cite20†this https URL†mednugget-ai.de access is available upon request.}, a tool for query-driven extraction and clustering of information nuggets from medical documents to support clinicians in exploring underlying medical evidence. Backed by a large language model (LLM), \\textit{MedNuggetizer} performs repeated extractions of information nuggets that are then grouped to generate reliable evidence within and across multiple documents.\nL41: We demonstrate its utility on the clinical use case of \\textit{antibiotic prophylaxis before prostate biopsy} by using major urological guidelines and recent PubMed studies as sources of information. Evaluation by domain experts shows that \\textit{MedNuggetizer} provides clinicians and researchers with an efficient way to explore long documents and easily extract reliable, query-focused medical evidence.\nL42: Comments: Preprint accepted at ECIR 2026\nL43: Subjects: Information Retrieval (cs.IR)\nL44: Cite as: cite21†arXiv:2512.15384 [cs.IR]\nL45:   (or  cite22†arXiv:2512.15384v1 [cs.IR] for this version)\nL46:   cite23†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2512.15384†doi.org L47: \nL48: Focus to learn more\nL49: \nL50:   arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL51: ## Submission history\nL52: \nL53: From: Gregor Donabauer [cite24†view email ]\nL54: [v1] Wed, 17 Dec 2025 12:37:44 UTC (657 KB)\nL55: \nL56: Full-text links:\nL57: ## Access Paper:\nL58: \nL59:  View a PDF of the paper titled MedNuggetizer: Confidence-Based Information Nugget Extraction from Medical Documents, by Gregor Donabauer and 8 other authors\nL60: \nL61:   * cite18†View PDF L62:   * cite19†HTML (experimental) L63:   * cite25†TeX Source  L64: \nL65: cite26† view license †creativecommons.org L66: \nL67: Current browse context:\nL68: \nL69: cs.IR\nL70: \nL71: cite27†< prev |   cite28†next > L72: \nL73: cite29†new |  cite30†recent | cite31†2025-12 L74: \nL75: Change to browse by:\nL76: \nL77: cite32†cs L78: ### References & Citations\nL79: \