ational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L163: \nL164: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2512.15231v1] CangLing-KnowFlow: A Unified Knowledge-and-Flow-fused Agent for Comprehensive Remote Sensing Applications (https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15231v1)\nciteturn6520view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15231v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 163\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 17 Dec 2025 (this version), latest version 4 Jun 2026 (cite5†v3 )]\nL9: # Title:CangLing-KnowFlow: A Unified Knowledge-and-Flow-fused Agent for Comprehensive Remote Sensing Applications\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Zhengchao Chen , cite7†Haoran Wang , cite8†Jing Yao , cite9†Pedram Ghamisi , cite10†Jun Zhou , cite11†Peter M. Atkinson , cite12†Bing Zhang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled CangLing-KnowFlow: A Unified Knowledge-and-Flow-fused Agent for Comprehensive Remote Sensing Applications, by Zhengchao Chen and 6 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite13†View PDF cite14†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:The automated and intelligent processing of massive remote sensing (RS) datasets is critical in Earth observation (EO). Existing automated systems are normally task-specific, lacking a unified framework to manage diverse, end-to-end workflows--from data preprocessing to advanced interpretation--across diverse RS applications.\nL17: To address this gap, this paper introduces CangLing-KnowFlow, a unified intelligent agent framework that integrates a Procedural Knowledge Base (PKB), Dynamic Workflow Adjustment, and an Evolutionary Memory Module. The PKB, comprising 1,008 expert-validated workflow cases across 162 practical RS tasks, guides planning and substantially reduces hallucinations common in general-purpose agents.\nL18: During runtime failures, the Dynamic Workflow Adjustment autonomously diagnoses and replans recovery strategies, while the Evolutionary Memory Module continuously learns from these events, iteratively enhancing the agent's knowledge and performance. This synergy enables CangLing-KnowFlow to adapt, learn, and operate reliably across diverse, complex tasks.\nL19: We evaluated CangLing-KnowFlow on the KnowFlow-Bench, a novel benchmark of 324 workflows inspired by real-world applications, testing its performance across 13 top Large Language Model (LLM) backbones, from open-source to commercial. Across all complex tasks, CangLing-KnowFlow surpassed the Reflexion baseline by at least 4% in Task Success Rate.\nL20: As the first most comprehensive validation along this emerging field, this research demonstrates the great potential of CangLing-KnowFlow as a robust, efficient, and scalable automated solution for complex EO challenges by leveraging expert knowledge (Knowledge) into adaptive and verifiable procedures (Flow).\nL21: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite15†arXiv:2512.15231 [cs.AI]\nL23:    | (or cite16†arXiv:2512.15231v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL24:    | cite17†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2512.15231†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Jing Yao [cite18†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Wed, 17 Dec 2025 09:31:57 UTC (6,932 KB)\nL29: cite19†[v2] Mon, 5 Jan 2026 15:48:10 UTC (5,834 KB)\nL30: cite5†[v3] Thu, 4 Jun 2026 07:06:20 UTC (5,757 KB)\nL31: \nL32: Full-text links:\nL33: \nL34: ## Access Paper:\nL35: \nL36: View a PDF of the paper titled CangLing-KnowFlow: A Unified Knowledge-and-Flow-fused Agent for Comprehensive Remote Sensing Applications, by Zhengchao 